    "result_text": "The full suite consists of one test class (the other two files are support classes), and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented membership level 4, gated on owner tenure, in the `Owner` entity \u2014 the single place membership level is derived.\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**\n- Raised `MAX_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL` from 3 to 4 and added a `MEMBERSHIP_TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS = 365` constant.\n- Added tenure as a fourth additive factor in `getMembershipLevel()`: base 1, +1 for email, +1 for no namesakes, +1 for qualifying tenure, capped at 4.\n- Extracted a small `hasQualifyingTenure()` helper (single responsibility, mirroring the existing `hasEmail()` helper) that returns true only when more than 365 days have elapsed since `registrationDate` (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`), returning false when there's no registration date.\n- Updated the Javadoc; added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n- Updated the `membershipLevel` schema `maximum` to 4 and refreshed the description.\n\nBecause a newly created owner has zero tenure, `hasQualifyingTenure()` is false, so a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 scores 1+1+1 = **3, never 4** \u2014 matching the spec and the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test.\n\nThe `householdSize` mentioned in the spec example is not a scoring factor (it never was in the existing additive rules); the example simply describes a complete new-owner record whose pre-tenure factors are maxed, confirming it still caps at 3.",
